# Aurora-Pulse

Match-3 / Triple Mahjong puzzle for [Devfest Hackathon](https://www.devfest.ru/program/2dc181dc-2adf-47bf-af8d-b80f43d16fd2/).

## Stack

- **Engine (dev):** Godot 4.x, GDScript
- **Target:** Aurora OS (Sailfish-derived), touch-only, no physical keyboard in release build
- **Repo:** https://github.com/Geraa50/Aurora-Pulse

## Hackathon requirements (must ship)

1. At least one **completed level** (win/lose loop, restart)
2. **Touch-only** input — tap/drag; keyboard only in editor debug if needed
3. **Feedback:** score, stars, progress bar, or level counter
4. **Assets:** original or clearly licensed (CC0 / open); keep `docs/ASSETS.md`

## Game design (Triple Mahjong)

- Board: stacked/layered tiles (classic mahjong solitaire layout, simplified for MVP)
- Player selects **3 identical** free tiles → they clear
- Tile **free** if nothing on top and at least one long side open
- Win: board empty. Lose: no valid triples left (optional shuffle/hint later)

## Code layout

- `game/` — Godot project root (`project.godot`)
- `game/scripts/` — gameplay (`board`, `tile`, `level`, `game_manager`)
- `game/scenes/` — UI + level scenes
- `game/assets/` — art/audio + licenses
- `docs/DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md` — roadmap
- `features/` — DAE specs (when using disciplined-agentic-engineering)

## Porting notes (Aurora)

- Keep input in one `TouchInput` / UI layer; no hard dependency on desktop keys
- Prefer Control-based UI over raw `_input` for Sailfish gestures
- Plan Aurora package (RPM/QML shell or Godot export template) in phase 4 of dev plan
